    "title": "Missing eGFR and LFTs for TDF monitoring",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR every 12 months for experienced patients on TDF, and LFTs plus RFTs when TDF toxicity signs are present. Patient has been on TDF for 6 years; today's labs include creatinine but no eGFR was calculated or documented. No LFTs were ordered despite musculoskeletal symptoms potentially attributable to TDF. The clinician's plan does not include eGFR calculation, LFTs, or any renal toxicity workup. Serum phosphate was checked and is low, further increasing the need for a full renal and hepatic evaluation per guideline toxicity management.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
