    "alert_id": "NSAID_TDF_NEPHROTOXICITY",
    "title": "Ibuprofen plus TDF increases renal risk",
    "message": "Guidelines identify TDF as a cause of acute kidney injury and Fanconi syndrome. Concurrent use of NSAIDs such as ibuprofen with TDF compounds nephrotoxic risk, particularly in a patient already showing signs of possible proximal tubular dysfunction (low phosphate, trace proteinuria). Patient uses over-the-counter ibuprofen regularly for chronic back pain. Uncontrolled hypertension (146/94) adds further renal stress. The clinician's plan recommends PRN ibuprofen without flagging the combined renal risk with TDF and hypertension.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Counsel patient to limit ibuprofen use. Consider alternative analgesia (e.g., paracetamol). Monitor renal function closely and evaluate for TDF-related tubular toxicity.",
